Hi Daniel,

I attached the tools usually included in the FW release for both version 1.=
0.59.59 v003F and 1.0.76.76 v0061.
Here is briefing of the tools:
        fullimage_update - update the configuration in the fullimage
        start_cfg - compile the start config (pre-configuration)

In start_cfg, you can check the file cfg_in_seq_attached.c.
All the host API described in the CHM files (I sent last time) can be used =
in this file.
They are invoked in sequence during system boot up.
Run "mk.sh" to compile it into a binary file - start_cfg.bin.
Then use command " ./fullimage_update --start-cfg start_cfg.bin 16384 f48x_=
full_image.bin" to generate a new fullimage file.

You can play with it and let me know if you have questions.

Thanks & Regards,
Xu Liang

